{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/649199-tatterdemalion-kith","id":649199,"title":"Tatterdemalion Kith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-02T12:49:49-07:00","id":649199,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Tatterdemalion Kith","content":"For an elemental seeming (CtL), or type of hobgoblin, would it be far-fetched to base one around garments? I got the idea from a D&amp;D monster called a &quot;tatterdemalion&quot;. They're basically discarded or used clothes, jewelry, etc. that gain a semblance of life. For a blessing, I'm wondering if it'd be better if they could detach pieces of themselves as a form of escape. The other idea would be to cause subtle suggestion to a host if they're &quot;equipped&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T17:21:41-07:00","id":649554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/649199-tatterdemalion-kith#post649199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For an elemental seeming (CtL), or type of hobgoblin, would it be far-fetched to base one around garments? I got the idea from a D&amp;D monster called a &quot;tatterdemalion&quot;. They're basically discarded or used clothes, jewelry, etc. that gain a semblance of life. For a blessing, I'm wondering if it'd be better if they could detach pieces of themselves as a form of escape. The other idea would be to cause subtle suggestion to a host if they're &quot;equipped&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> For a hobgoblin type, I'm guessing tatterdemalions would be a sub-type of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tsukumogami\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Tsukumogami</b></a>, or just enchanted and sapient objects in general.<br /> <br /> As a Kith, it doesn't have to follow 1ed rules. Clothes can be of so many styles, and a Seeming refines the visual into something personal. Here's my take:<br /> <br /> Beast: Mink coats, feather hats, reptilian leather, jewelry made of fireflies. Transgressive, avant-garde and iconoclast features are very frequent. Some of them might have parts of their bodies look naked even when covered, as flesh and fabric blur together. The strong scents, novel textures and primal sounds are imbued within and emanate from every thread.<br /> <br /> Darkling: Unobtrusive and usually muted colors, with a prevalence of Victorian and Gothic hues. Lots of practical features, like hidden pockets and holders. Dyed in tears and blood, woven out of night sky and whispering shadows.<br /> <br /> Elemental: Harmless and eye-catching manifestations of fitting elements, even those that are not solid at room temperature nor comfortable. There is a tendency for flashiness and a showy vigor. Philosophical phrases related to extrospection are common, be they written in normal words or a more abstract meta-language. These tatterdemalions rarely have uninteresting Miens.<br /> <br /> Fairest: Overlaps somewhat with Elementals, but the sense of admiration makes one look inward and imagine better ways of expressing oneself, rather than making one look at the world and appreciate the vastness of life. The fabrics and accessories tend to assume forms that are closer to mundane equivalents, but of amazing craftsmanship and exquisite detail.<br /> <br /> Ogre: Brutalism, minimalism and asceticism are the orders of the day. No more and no less, with comfort and ease of upkeep coming first. They run the gamut from armored biker jackets to the impeccable sleekness of a lab coat for no-nonsense scientists.<br /> <br /> Wizened: Defined more by ecletic mixtures of disparate styles than any coherent themes, they often give surrealist, cubist and psychedelic vibes. Expect them to carry their own tailor supplies and tools inside their bodies.<br /> <br /> Kith Blessing: Style Speaks. How you choose to dress yourself sends messages with varying degrees of subtlety, and Tatterdemalions excel in appreciating and investigating aesthetics. All rolls involving the appraisal, analysis, reviewing and the like of personal possessions, implicit or explicit messages in fashion choices and crafts receive 8 Again. These rolls usually involve Crafts, Expression, Investigation, Academics, Socialize and Empathy. Additionally, they may spend 1 point of glamour to enchant a personal belonging to contain a telepathic message for the rest of the scene. This follows the same rules as the <a href=\"http://www.thesubnet.com/portal/wod2/dtd/CreationEmVo.html\" target=\"_blank\"><b>&quot;Special Message&quot; Vocal Embed</b></a>, but no roll is necessary and the character automatically knows when the message has been received. She may enchant a number of personal belongings this way per scene equal to Wyrd. A different type of target may be specified for each enchanted object. They can all have the same message or any combination thereof.<br /> <br /> How does that sound?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 09-04-2015, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T17:44:54-07:00","id":649565,"title":"","content":"Very promising. I like the attention to detail you presented. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T17:45:14-07:00","id":650798,"title":"","content":"For 1e, perhaps the blessing could be a discount on Mirror Contracts? Sort of like how Manikins have it with Artifice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T21:07:29-07:00","id":650891,"title":"","content":"I'd recommend no. Mirrors is general already, while Artifice is Seeming, and Contract Discounts make poor Blessings anyway given unless you were planning to take it is is useless. GGF's idea would work well enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 09-04-2015, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T08:43:50-07:00","id":651270,"title":"","content":"Fair enough, either that or a discount in Contracts of Animation, maybe. Whatever sounds appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T10:20:27-07:00","id":651461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/649199-tatterdemalion-kith?p=651270#post651270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough, either that or a discount in Contracts of Animation, maybe. Whatever sounds appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, XP discounts, be it 1ed or 2ed, are unimpressive. After you buy all the 5 dots of Mirror or Artifice, that's it. If you want a benefit related to those Contracts, I'd say a +2 dice bonus for activation is better and would come up more often.<br /> <br /> If you wanna use Tatterdemalion as a 1ed kith, I'd say Elemental, Fairest and perhaps Wizened work as correspondent Seemings. If you plan on using Wyrd Evolution, Style Speaks grants 9 Again at character creation, but 8 Again once they reach Wyrd 7. Maybe you could give them a special and inherent Catch that waives the glamour cost of Contracts meant for transforming their clothes for stylistic reasons, rather than Stealth, Athletics and the like. They might need to roll Wyrd + Skill to get the style they are aiming for just right. That telepathic message ability sounds like it could be achieved easily with an alternative Contract clause for Fleeting Spring, Vainglory, Artifice or Communion With The Elements.<br /> <br /> Just my two cents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 09-04-2015, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T12:27:21-07:00","id":651617,"title":"","content":"I'd make it Elemental, but even in 1e the Seeming is not critical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T01:15:22-07:00","id":653626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/649199-tatterdemalion-kith#post649199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For an elemental seeming (CtL), or type of hobgoblin, would it be far-fetched to base one around garments? I got the idea from a D&amp;D monster called a &quot;tatterdemalion&quot;. They're basically discarded or used clothes, jewelry, etc. that gain a semblance of life. For a blessing, I'm wondering if it'd be better if they could detach pieces of themselves as a form of escape. The other idea would be to cause subtle suggestion to a host if they're &quot;equipped&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>For an alternate presentation (besides the D&amp;D one) on the tatterdemalion, take a look at Terry Brooks' <b>Knight of the Word</b> (second book of his &quot;Word and Void&quot; series). There, a tatterdemalion is a fae creature pieced together from the hopes, dreams, and fears of the lost, the children whom no one ever looked for . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}